(version 1)

# A bypass capacitor wants the lowest inductance it can get to
# the plane, so a thermal relief on one works against the reason
# it is there. Through-hole pads keep their reliefs so the
# terminals stay hand-solderable.
(rule "surface-mount pads connect solid"
	(constraint zone_connection solid)
	(condition "A.Pad_Type == 'SMD'"))

# One spoke is enough on a through-hole ground pad, because the
# spokes are not what connects it. Ground is routed as a net
# (see tools/autoroute.py), so every ground pad already has its
# own track, and the pour only adds area. KiCad wants two by
# default, and on a D-sub - where signal tracks crowd between
# the pins - the router often leaves room for one; that failed
# DRC as an error on a different D-sub pin on each routing run.
# A bare count, not (min 1): the (min ...) form is for
# distances. Written that way, KiCad threw the whole file away
# without a word, and the SMD rule above went with it.
# SP_ACM, the VFD side's common, is routed and poured the
# same way, so the same holds for it.
(rule "through-hole ground pads need one spoke"
	(constraint min_resolved_spokes 1)
	(condition "A.Pad_Type == 'Through-hole' && (A.NetName == 'GND' || A.NetName == 'SP_ACM')"))
